428	Facts about the data, confirmed on real repositories:
429	
430	- **Refs layout:** each ref `refs/entire/checkpoints/<shard>/<id>` points at a commit whose tree has `metadata.json` and `<n>/metadata.json`, `<n>/prompt.txt`, `<n>/transcript.jsonl`, `<n>/full.jsonl` for session index `n`.
431	- **Branch layout:** branch `entire/checkpoints/v1` has the same content under `<first two chars of id>/<rest of id>/`.
432	- **Root `metadata.json`:** `checkpoint_id`, `branch`, `sessions[]`, `token_usage`.
433	- **Session `metadata.json`:** `session_id`, `created_at`, `agent`, `model`, `branch`, `files_touched[]`, `token_usage{input_tokens,output_tokens,cache_read_tokens,cache_creation_tokens}`, `session_metrics.turn_count`.
434	- **`transcript.jsonl`:** one JSON object per line: `{ type: 'user' | 'assistant', ts, content: [...] }`.
435	  - user blocks: `{ id, text }`; blocks with `type: 'image'` are skipped.
436	  - assistant blocks: `{ type: 'text', text }` or `{ type: 'tool_use', id, name, input, result? }` where `result` is `{ output: string, status: 'success' | string }`.
437	- **Commit link:** a commit body line `Entire-Checkpoint: <id>`.
438	
439	Parsing rules:
440	
441	- A user text block becomes a `user` entry. An assistant text block becomes an `assistant` entry.
442	- A `tool_use` block becomes a `tool_call` entry (`toolName`, `toolUseId`, `command = input.command` when it is a string, `filePath = input.file_path` when it is a string, `text = JSON.stringify(input)` cut to 4000 characters). When `result` exists it is followed by a `tool_result` entry with the same `toolName` and `toolUseId`, `isError = result.status !== 'success'`.
443	- Tool output is stripped of ANSI escape codes and, when longer than 8000 characters, reduced to its first 3000 and last 5000 characters joined by `\n…[truncated]…\n`. Test summaries sit at the end, so the tail is kept longer.
444	- Every `text` and `command` passes through `redact`.
445	- A session keeps at most 5000 entries. A malformed line is skipped, not fatal.
446	- `startedAt` is the first entry timestamp, else `created_at`. `endedAt` is the last entry timestamp.
447	- A session is inside the window when `startedAt <= until` and `(endedAt ?? startedAt) >= since`. Keep the newest `maxSessions` (default 12).
448	- The same `session_id` appearing in several checkpoints is merged: keep the longest transcript, union the checkpoint ids and commits.
449	- `cloneOrUpdate`: a local path is used in place. A URL is cloned with `git clone --filter=blob:none` into `<dataDir>/repos/<owner>__<name>`, or fetched if present. Then `git fetch origin '+refs/entire/*:refs/entire/*'` and `git fetch origin '+refs/heads/entire/*:refs/remotes/origin/entire/*'`; a failure of either fetch is tolerated.
450	- `ingest` throws `NoCheckpointsError` when no checkpoint ref exists. When checkpoints exist but none fall inside the window it returns an artifact with `sessions: []`.
451	- `diffs` holds `getDiff` output for every linked commit under keys `${sha}:${path}`, each patch cut to 6000 characters, at most 40 files per commit.
