560	### Task 4: Verification rules and the grounding gate
561	
562	**Files:** `packages/verify/src/**`, `packages/verify/test/**`
563	
564	**Interfaces:**
565	- Consumes: `Session`, `Entry`, `Claim`, `Line`, `Facts`, `DiffIndex`, `EvidenceRef` from `@dailies/core`.
566	- Produces:
567	```ts
568	export type CommandClass = 'test' | 'build' | 'typecheck' | 'lint' | 'other';
569	export type RunOutcome = 'pass' | 'fail' | 'unknown';
570	export interface ToolRun { callEntryId: string; resultEntryId: string | null; index: number; command: string; cls: CommandClass; outcome: RunOutcome }
571	export function classifyCommand(command: string): CommandClass
572	export function parseOutcome(cls: CommandClass, output: string, isError: boolean): RunOutcome
573	export function collectRuns(session: Session): ToolRun[]
574	export function normalize(text: string): string                       // collapse whitespace, drop * _ ` marks
575	export function quoteMatches(quote: string, text: string): boolean
576	export function verifyClaim(claim: Claim, session: Session): Claim    // sets verdict, reason, evidence; leaves 'implemented' untouched
577	export function verifyClaims(claims: Claim[], sessions: Session[]): Claim[]
578	export function lintStyle(text: string): string[]                     // empty array means clean
579	export function checkLine(line: Line, ctx: { sessions: Session[]; facts: Facts; diffs: DiffIndex }, o?: { skipStyle?: boolean }): { ok: boolean; reasons: string[] }
580	```
581	
582	Rules:
583	
584	- **`classifyCommand`.** Split the command on `&&`, `||`, `;` and `|`; classify each part; return the first non-`other` class in the order test, typecheck, lint, build.
585	  - test: `vitest`, `jest`, `pytest`, `mocha`, `playwright test`, `go test`, `cargo test`, `dotnet test`, `rspec`, `phpunit`, `python -m unittest`, `<npm|pnpm|yarn|bun> [run] test`, `make test`.
586	  - typecheck: `tsc`, `mypy`, `pyright`.
587	  - lint: `eslint`, `biome`, `ruff`, `flake8`, `<pm> [run] lint`.
588	  - build: `<pm> [run] build`, `next build`, `vite build`, `cargo build`, `go build`, `make` or `make build`.
589	- **`parseOutcome`.** Strip ANSI codes first. `isError` true gives `fail`.
590	  - test: `fail` on `(\d+) (failed|failing)` with a count above zero, on `Tests?:\s+\d+ failed`, on a line starting `FAIL`, on `AssertionError`. `pass` when there is no fail marker and one of `(\d+) passed`, a line starting `PASS`, a line starting `ok ` followed by a package path, `test result: ok`. Otherwise `unknown`.
591	  - typecheck: `fail` on `error TS\d+` or `Found [1-9]\d* errors?`; `pass` on `Found 0 errors` or empty output; otherwise `unknown`.
592	  - lint and build: `pass` on empty output or `compiled successfully`, `built in`, `Done in`, `0 errors`, `0 problems`; `fail` on `[1-9]\d* errors?` or `[1-9]\d* problems?`; otherwise `unknown`.
593	- **`collectRuns`.** Every `tool_call` entry with a `command` whose class is not `other`, paired with the `tool_result` entry sharing its `toolUseId`. No result entry gives `outcome: 'unknown'`.
594	- **`tests_pass`.** Consider test runs before the claim's entry. None: `unverifiable`, reason `no test run is recorded before this message`. Last run `fail`: `contradicted`. Last run `unknown`: `unverifiable`. Last run `pass`: if a `tool_call` with `toolName` in `Edit`, `Write`, `MultiEdit`, `NotebookEdit` and a `filePath` not ending in `.md` sits between that run and the claim, `stale` with the edit as evidence; else `verified`. Evidence is the run's call and result entries.
595	- **`build_passes`.** The same over runs of class `build` or `typecheck`.
596	- **`ran_command`.** Find the last `tool_call` before the claim whose normalised command contains the normalised `subject`. None: `unverifiable`. Its result `isError`: `contradicted`. Otherwise `verified`.
597	- **`fixed_error`.** Find the first `tool_result` containing the normalised `subject`. None: `unverifiable`. Take the last later run before the claim with the same command class. None: `unverifiable`. Its output still contains the subject or its outcome is `fail`: `contradicted`. Otherwise `verified`.
598	- A claim whose `quote` does not match its entry by `quoteMatches` gets `unverifiable` with reason `quote not found in transcript`. Callers drop such claims; the rule here is the safety net.
599	- **`lintStyle`.** Returns a reason for: more than one sentence; more than 26 words; an em dash or an exclamation mark; a number written as a word from `one` to `twenty`; any banned phrase from `delve`, `seamless`, `robust`, `leverage`, `cutting-edge`, `game-changer`, `dive into`, `unleash`, `supercharge`, `effortless`, `revolutioniz`, `it's worth noting`, `not just`.
600	- **`checkLine`.** Fails with a reason when: an `entry` ref names an unknown entry, or its `quote` does not match that entry; a `diff` ref names a key missing from `diffs`, or its `quote` is not in that patch; a `stat` ref names a key missing from `facts`; a number in the line text (`\d+(?:\.\d+)?`) is neither the value of a referenced stat nor present in a referenced entry or patch; `lintStyle` reports anything (unless `skipStyle` is set).
